              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Leila"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the best. I used pineapple chunks because that's what I had, and I used the juice because that's how other watergate salad recipes are written. The coconut and cherries are great in this. I also added chopped walnuts. I think next time I will quarter rather than halve the cherries to cut down on those super sweet bites.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-09T17:59:52.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stlrgrl72"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for a family function today. It was a hit! I only have about 1/2 of a serving left. I made 2 changes to this recipe: I did not drain the pineapple and I only used an 8 oz container of whipped topping. My mom even asked for the recipe :)",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-23T19:24:38.307Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CRYSTALSHOE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As the recipe was written, it was just average. After making it and letting it sit for a few hours, I decided to add more fruit (bananas, clementines, and extra cherries), and more whipped topping to keep it creamy. The extra fruit really added a lot of flavor and texture to it. I have had versions of this with only the pinapple &amp; coconut, but they seemed better than this recipe- I'm not sure why.",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-03T12:38:39.427Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RECIPESEEKER1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I previously had 2 different written recipes of Watergate salad, but wanted to find the real one - this is it! I followed this, only added in a can of drained mandarin orages for more fruit. However, it was more white than green, and couldn't taste the pistachio, so I think I will add a second box of pudding next time. Had lots of compliments at my church group.",
            "datePublished": "2008-03-27T11:52:45.443Z"
          },
